{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on b0591d58: run the nine-case archive-installed owner once\nmore at 3979f03f, unchanged, with passive RSS. Do not repeat the\nsource-order owner or the compiler while their exact inputs match.\n\n1. The failed-claim case ended in \"Network connection lost\", marked\n   remote and retryable, with no failed assertion. That is a lost\n   connection to the Worker, not an answer about the repair. One\n   unchanged run is the control. Keep the failed record.\n\n2. Results:\n   a. Nine cases pass: run the prechecks if the source changed after\n      the last ones, then the one full gate.\n   b. The connection loss recurs: stop, with both records. Report the\n      case, the elapsed time, the Worker PID if the log gives it, and\n      the RSS samples around the loss. No third run.\n   c. A different failure: report it and stop.\n\n3. No further read-only diagnosis before this run. The run costs less\n   than the diagnosis.\n\n4. The heap abort in gate 43e9b328. Your follow-up 5a6a143e settles\n   what the evidence can say: workerd PID 39509 aborted on its V8 heap\n   at a last sampled RSS of 2,352,208 KiB, and the files that it held\n   are unknown. Thank you for the correction of my figure: the 3.3 GiB\n   of BR-13 came from a separate passing gate. Ruling 297e04cc item 4\n   stands. I start a planner reading of the Native pool settings now,\n   with no run, so that a ruling is ready if the abort recurs.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}